Subject: [PATCH 3/4] =?UTF-8?q?fork(lhc):=20Chunk=202=20=E2=80=94=20infere?=
 =?UTF-8?q?nce=20adapter,=20request-context=20serving,=20compact=20bridge?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20with=20write-back?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

LHC now compacts. Behind GROK_LHC (off by default; host behaviourally identical
when unset, with no added per-turn work). Six marked core touchpoints, sentinel
enforced. 141 lib + 71 certification + 5 golden tests, tripwire green.

This supersedes the partial implementation swept into 9d7922a. That commit is
labelled "review" but also contains pre-fix Chunk 2 code with known critical
defects, because it was made with `git add -A`. I intended to reset and reland
it as one honest commit — Lee approved that, conditional on it being unpushed.
It was already pushed. Pushed history on this fork is never rewritten, so
9d7922a stays and this commit lands on top of it. Read the two together.

What this adds on top of Chunk 1's capture:
- LHC inference adapter: per-call credential refresh, cancellation, dedicated
  model override, typed error classification.
- Request-context serving (hook 4), instrumented-redundant per Lee's ruling —
  it stays through Chunk 2 gathering equivalence evidence and comes out at
  Chunk 3 if that evidence shows zero divergence.
- Compact bridge with WRITE-BACK: LHC's compacted body is written back into
  native state via the host's own replace_conversation_for_compaction. Ruled the
  proven LHC-host architecture (pi-lhc, t3code); serving-without-write-back was
  the deviation that caused the two-truths failure mode — token accounting never
  decreased and fail-open landed on an oversized body.

Design change ratified mid-chunk: classification moved from parsing rendered
text to typed provenance from get_session_thread_view. The prefix-based
classifier produced a new defect in three consecutive rounds — desync in the
DEFAULT compact mode, image-bearing prompts failing to match because
text_content() drops image parts while capture appends [image:...], and a
residual that misplaced a prompt_index marker and could corrupt cancelled-turn
rewind. Both acceptance verifiers returned DESIGN: SOUND; one argued it is
forced, since once rendered text is excluded the typed view's only remaining
discriminator is message_id provenance. Recorded as a binding Phase 4 law:
hosts never parse renders.

Serious defects caught and fixed during the chunk:
- The written-back body was not a fixpoint. LHC renders bands, tool results and
  runtime notes as User role, so each counted as a real user turn: markers
  landed on tool results, and every compaction re-stamped and re-recorded the
  same text. Caught by the ruled hard gate.
- Runtime notes round-tripped back as REAL user prompts, permanently promoting
  synthetic host items in the canonical record.
- get_classify_context turned a messages.list error into an EMPTY index and
  returned success — every real prompt would classify synthetic, erasing all
  markers and recapturing the user's own prompts as runtime_note.
- capture_active took a registry mutex every turn with GROK_LHC unset,
  violating off-by-default.
- The equivalence instrument was miscalibrated in both directions: informational
  divergence fired on cosmetic JSON whitespace on every tool window, while
  raw_fingerprint reduced a tool-call assistant to a constant and later collided
  on unescaped delimiters.

Live-tail kinds are conserved through write-back (tool_call, tool_result,
assistant_text, assistant_thinking, runtime_note, user_prompt); bands stay
user_meta because compaction prose is what compaction is. Two exceptions are
forced by host sink types and documented.

All 70 fingerprint contributions are individually pinned, jointly pinned, or
documented-redundant with a proof — verified by full deletion sweeps whose
survivors exactly equal the documented-redundant set.

17 rounds, dual adversarial verification throughout. Root causes of that count
are recorded in the onboarding doc: verifier sessions were started fresh each
round (so each assumed first contact and ran a maximal search) and the
orchestrator's stopping rule had no fixed point. Both fixed for Chunk 3.

Carried to Chunk 3 as named checkpoints: G2 (capture the real write-back body
from a live Replace compaction and re-verify instrument CALIBRATION, not just
fixtures); Chunk 1's session-id coupling and async-guard limitations; /btw and
memory flush on a compacted session; the hook-4 removal ruling.

patches/ regenerated across both chunk commits, all nine touchpoints, recovery
drill rehearsed (git am --3way onto a fresh clone applies clean).

